        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Of Crowns &amp; Chains </strong>is a solo-developed grand-strategy sandbox where every nation, army, and populace is dynamically simulated on a seamless spherical Earth. Lead a nation of your choice in January 1910 and influence the course of your nation as time marches onwards.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >IMPORTANT NOTE FROM THE SOLE DEVELOPER</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Since the game is in <strong>early</strong> <strong>Alpha</strong>, you may encounter <strong>bugs, optimization issues,</strong> and <strong>limited content </strong>(lacks navy system; no save/load system or deeper economy system, etc).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is an <strong>Early Access title</strong>, if you purchase this game, <strong>you will be getting access to the game in its</strong> <strong>current state.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you're<strong> </strong>unsure<strong>, please</strong> <strong>wait until the game transitions from Early Access to Full Release</strong> since the base game will be considered finished by then.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >CURRENT FEATURES</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Sphere World &amp; Accurate Landmass</strong> – No flat-map distortion. Landmasses are generated from real-world geospatial data; highly accurate coastlines and islands.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/d497543794d6dd22f7b50c2b55e90ae2.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/d497543794d6dd22f7b50c2b55e90ae2.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Resolution Modes</strong> – Procedurally generated tiles covers <strong>only Europe</strong> <i>(including Ottoman Empire, excluding Russia east of the Urals)</i>. You can select a tile resolution mode upon starting a <i>New Game </i>(no restart required). Historical states and provinces are not implemented; only procedural tiles.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The <strong>Normal </strong>tile density mode has the default tile resolution:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/2290bdd6172f5324fa9c7c5093facba9.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/2290bdd6172f5324fa9c7c5093facba9.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The <strong>Quad </strong>resolution mode features a 4x increase in tile resolution, offering better visuals and more accurate borders (also 4x GPU VRAM usage):</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/29b0535a7186c899002a1270e86d5aff.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/29b0535a7186c899002a1270e86d5aff.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Nation Selection </strong>– Choose any nation currently available, from the British Empire to the Ottoman Empire or the microstates of San Marino and Liechtenstein.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/a0d81a4b8e632eccd52df5fd2e072522.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/a0d81a4b8e632eccd52df5fd2e072522.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>National Treasury &amp; Debt System</strong> – Manage your nation's treasury by balancing hourly income from taxes and territory against the upkeep costs of your divisions. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/9aea69c14cc7ef703237e4f9ec920e41.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/9aea69c14cc7ef703237e4f9ec920e41.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unit System</strong> – Each unit represents a division (≈20,000 soldiers), with many divisions fitting inside a single tile.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/9e44b7829a751534bfb357e47ff78608.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/9e44b7829a751534bfb357e47ff78608.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Combat System</strong> – Battles can last for days under certain conditions. There are three hidden phases of combat—Skirmish, Assault, and Breach (battle reports not implemented). Divisions get exhausted during combat and newly captured tiles must be consolidated.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/4c435ddea690da18dae2ee43f116af57.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/4c435ddea690da18dae2ee43f116af57.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dynamic Population &amp; Manpower</strong> – Populations grow, age, and decline over time. Casualties directly impact age distribution, while manpower pools adjust as soldiers retire or new recruits become eligible. Demographic change is simulated realistically in backend code (infant mortality, fertility rates, gender).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/166b17d35ff10f1ec6f509ff478978ee.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"width=1019 height=573 /></span></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Wars, Ceasefires &amp; Limited Alliances</strong> –  Occupy tiles and declare wars. Cascading calls-to-arms can pull suzerains, vassals and allies into conflict; tiles can be occupied and liberated. Alliances cannot be negotiated (only historical alliances are active on game start).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/300c6d6d529671a0dc6e05d3b512f0f1.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/300c6d6d529671a0dc6e05d3b512f0f1.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li></ul>",
