ower</strong> – Populations grow, age, and decline over time. Casualties directly impact age distribution, while manpower pools adjust as soldiers retire or new recruits become eligible. Demographic change is simulated realistically in backend code (infant mortality, fertility rates, gender).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/166b17d35ff10f1ec6f509ff478978ee.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"width=1019 height=573 /></span></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Wars, Ceasefires &amp; Limited Alliances</strong> –  Occupy tiles and declare wars. Cascading calls-to-arms can pull suzerains, vassals and allies into conflict; tiles can be occupied and liberated. Alliances cannot be negotiated (only historical alliances are active on game start).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras/300c6d6d529671a0dc6e05d3b512f0f1.avif?t=1774813260\" alt=\"\"data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3867100/extras_big/300c6d6d529671a0dc6e05d3b512f0f1.webp?t=1774813260 width=1560 height=877 /></span></p></li></ul>",
